# androdr-049 is a patch-level (device_posture) rule: EXPOSED, never DETECTED (Q9-3).
# Requires a patch level old enough that the rule's CVEs are unpatched. In a --load run
# with mercenary_predator_artifacts or mercenary_dns_c2 the Predator row is DETECTED
# (DETECTED outranks EXPOSED), so the EXPOSED lines can only hold without them.
[!!]  Predator: EXPOSED --
~\[!!\]  Predator: EXPOSED -- [0-9]+ CVEs linked to Predator \(unpatched; not evidence of infection\)
# A CVE rule must never read as DETECTED.
!~Predator: DETECTED -- .*CVEs linked to
